# Local CI after each task

After finishing an implementation, fix, or other repo-changing task, run `./scripts/ci.sh` from the repo root **once**. Do not run it after every individual file edit.

That script is the same gate as GitHub Actions: `cargo fmt --check`, `clippy -D warnings`, `build`, `test`, and `gitleaks`.

- If fmt fails, run `cargo fmt --all`, then re-run `./scripts/ci.sh`.
- If anything else fails, fix it and re-run until the script exits 0.
- Do not declare the task done while CI is red.
- Skip only when the task made no repo changes (questions, explanations).
- Propose the git commit message after CI is green.
